IAM principle:


    Least privilege.


Known platform limitation:


    Floci did not fully reproduce the expected AWS IAM
    authorization boundaries during the tested S3
    operations.


The intended policy design remains least privilege.


The architecture was NOT weakened simply to accommodate
emulator behavior.


================================================================================
PHASE 2 — CLOUD INCIDENTS
================================================================================

INC-001
-------

Title:


    Floci State Loss / Persistence Misconfiguration


Summary:


    Floci cloud resources appeared to be lost after
    changing Docker Compose configuration.


Root cause:


    The new Compose configuration referenced different
    storage rather than the existing Floci application state.


Resolution:


    Identify the existing persistent storage and explicitly
    bind the Floci deployment to the correct volume.


Operational lesson:


    A Docker volume being present does not automatically
    mean the application is using the correct volume.


Document:


    docs/incidents/INC-001-floci-state-loss.md


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
INC-002
-------

Title:


    Floci Lambda Execution Failure


Summary:


    Lambda invocation failed because Floci could not
    communicate with the Docker daemon from inside
    the Floci container.


Root cause:


    Floci Lambda execution requires Docker access.


Observed:


    unix:///var/run/docker.sock


Resolution:


    Mount the host Docker socket into the Floci container.


Verification:


    [x] Docker socket visible inside Floci
    [x] Lambda container created
    [x] Lambda container started
    [x] Lambda invocation successful
    [x] SQS event source successfully invoked Lambda


Document:


    docs/incidents/INC-002-floci-lambda-exec-failure


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
INC-003
-------

Status:


    DOCUMENTED


INC-003 is part of the Phase 2 cloud incident history.

The detailed incident record in the repository is the
source of truth for its exact investigation, root cause,
resolution and operational lesson.


Important:


    Do not reconstruct incident details from memory
    when the repository documentation is available.


