Troubleshooting principle:


    Failures encountered during implementation are treated
    as part of the engineering process.


Investigation and root-cause analysis are documented
rather than hidden or worked around without explanation.


================================================================================
DOCUMENTATION
================================================================================

Documentation model:


    architecture
        =
    what the system is and why it is designed this way


    infrastructure
        =
    what is actually deployed


    procedures
        =
    how to perform administrative tasks


    incidents / troubleshooting
        =
    failures, investigation, root cause and resolution


    software
        =
    software inventory and licensing


    cloud
        =
    cloud-specific implementation


    security
        =
    security controls and practices


    disaster-recovery
        =
    backup and recovery


Documentation principle:


    Documentation follows implementation.

    Planned documentation is not treated as completed
    documentation.

    Each phase is documented after the implemented state
    has been verified.


