================================================================================
IMPORTANT PROJECT RULES
================================================================================

    1. Implementation comes before theory.


    2. Learn concepts when they become necessary.


    3. Verify everything important.


    4. Troubleshooting is part of engineering.


    5. Documentation describes actual state.


    6. Do not mark work complete merely because
       configuration was planned.


    7. Do not introduce unnecessary infrastructure.


    8. Do not commit secrets or machine-sensitive state.


    9. Prefer reproducible scripts and documentation
       over VM-state artifacts.


    10. Update project state after meaningful milestones.


    11. Update roadmap after meaningful milestones.


    12. Keep the repository as the implementation
        source of truth.


    13. Keep the master context as the project-state
        and architectural source of truth.


    14. Do not start Phase 4 until Phase 3 documentation
        and closeout are complete.


